1. To Install Virtualbox / VMware Workstation with different flavours of linux or windows OS.
- Download the VirtualBox executable file and click it.
- Click the "Next" button through the setup wizard screens.
- Click the "Yes" button when warned about Network Interfaces.
- Click the "Install" button to begin installation.
- Once the installation is completed, the VirtualBox icon will be shown on the desktop screen.

2. To Install a C compiler in the virtual machine created using virtual box and executes Simple Program.
- Open VirtualBox and navigate to File -> Import Appliance.
- Browse and select the ubuntu_gt6.ova file.
- Go to settings, select USB, and choose USB 1.1.
- Start the ubuntu_gt6 virtual machine.
- Open the terminal in Ubuntu.
- Type `cd /opt/axis2/axis2-1.7.3/bin` and press enter.
- Type `gedit first.c` to open the text editor and enter your C program.
- Type `gcc first.c` to compile the program.
- Type `./a.out` to execute the program and display the output.

3. Create EC2 Instance in AWS (Amazon)
- Log into your AWS account and click on “services” on the primary screen, then select “EC2” under Compute.
- Click on “Launch instance” and provide a name for the instance (e.g., My Web Server).
- Select the required operating system from the Application and OS Images (AMI) catalog.
- Keep the default instance type as “t2.micro” (Free tier eligible).
- Create or select a key pair (e.g., .pem file) to securely connect to the instance.
- Keep network settings as default and ensure storage is within the free tier limit (up to 30 GB EBS).
- Click on “Launch instance”.
- To connect, select your running server, click the connect button, and copy the provided SSH key command.
- Open your local terminal, navigate to the folder with your .pem key, and paste the SSH command to connect.

4. To develop a simple custom application using the Apex programming language on the Salesforce cloud platform.
- Sign up for a free Salesforce Developer Org and log in with your credentials.
- Open the Developer Console by clicking the gear icon (Setup) and selecting Developer Console.
- Navigate to File > New > Apex Class, enter a name (e.g., HelloWorldApp), and click OK.
- Write the following Apex code and save the class (File > Save):
    public class HelloWorldApp {
        public static void sayHello() {
            System.debug('WELCOME TO APEX PROGRAMMING');
        }
    }
- Click the Debug menu and select Open Execute Anonymous Window.
- Enter the following code, ensure "Open Log" is checked, and click Execute:
    HelloWorldApp.sayHello();
- Select the "Debug Only" checkbox in the execution log to view the output message.

5. Implement a mailing service using Apex programming language of salesforce.com
- Open the Developer Console from the quick access menu in Salesforce.
- Click File > New > Apex Class, enter “EmailManager” as the class name, and click OK.
- Replace the default body with the email service code and click File > Save:
    public class EmailManager {
        public void sendMail(String address, String subject, String body) {
            Messaging.SingleEmailMessage mail = new Messaging.SingleEmailMessage();
            String[] toAddresses = new String[] {address};
            mail.setToAddresses(toAddresses);
            mail.setSubject(subject);
            mail.setPlainTextBody(body);
            Messaging.SendEmailResult[] results = Messaging.sendEmail(
                new Messaging.SingleEmailMessage[] { mail });
            inspectResults(results);
        }
        
        private static Boolean inspectResults(Messaging.SendEmailResult[] results) {
            Boolean sendResult = true;
            for (Messaging.SendEmailResult res : results) {
                if (res.isSuccess()) {
                    System.debug('Email sent successfully');
                } else {
                    sendResult = false;
                    System.debug('The following errors occurred: ' + res.getErrors());
                }
            }
            return sendResult;
        }
    }
- Click Debug > Open Execute Anonymous Window and enter the following to test, then click Execute:
    EmailManager em = new EmailManager();
    em.sendMail('Your email address', 'Email Subject', 'Email Body');

